{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:102399",
  "title": "Important: freerdp security update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-25 00:05:01"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-26 00:06:43"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "FreeRDP is a free implementation of the Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP), released under the Apache license. The xfreerdp client can connect to RDP servers such as Microsoft Windows machines, xrdp, and VirtualBox.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via file descriptor exhaustion in serial device handling (CVE-2026-110830)\n\n* FreeRDP: FreeRDP before 3.32.2 Certificate Identity Validation Bypass via tls_verify_certificate (CVE-2026-121392)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Memory corruption via race condition in planar bitmap decoding (CVE-2026-121957)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Arbitrary code execution via RD Gateway RPC client heap buffer overflow (CVE-2026-121964)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Use-after-free via rdpgfx dynamic virtual channel close (CVE-2026-121953)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
